                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Count cases with 0, 1 or 2 twenty-cent pieces.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "With no 20-cent pieces, the number of 10-cent pieces can be 0 to 5: 6 ways.\nWith one 20-cent piece, 30 cents remains, giving 0 to 3 ten-cent pieces: 4 ways.\nWith two 20-cent pieces, 10 cents remains, giving 0 or 1 ten-cent piece: 2 ways.\nIn each case the remaining amount determines the number of 5-cent pieces.\n$$6+4+2=12$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q9b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many ways can you make change for 100 dollars using 5, 10, 20 and 50 dollar notes?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p3-q9b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "49",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p3-q9b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Count cases with 0, 1 or 2 fifty-dollar notes.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "With no 50-dollar notes, use 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5 twenty-dollar notes. The remaining amounts are 100, 80, 60, 40, 20 and 0 dollars. These allow respectively 11, 9, 7, 5, 3 and 1 choices for the number of 10-dollar notes; the remaining amount fixes the number of 5-dollar notes.\n$$11+9+7+5+3+1=36$$\nWith one 50-dollar note, the remaining 50 dollars can be made in $6+4+2=12$ ways.\nWith two 50-dollar notes, there is 1 way.\n$$36+12+1=49$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
